# UCOS-RFP-001 W2-00 P-01 (RFP-1 / CLO-01 / CLO-05) — git bundle archives. A bundle is a
# version-control TRANSPORT container: a serialization of the object database, produced by
# `git bundle create` for backup or offline transfer. It is an environment output, so
# RFP-001's class_derivation places it in CLS-TRANSIENT at the first ordered question
# ("Is it absent from version control? → CLS-TRANSIENT if environment output"), and
# CLS-TRANSIENT is EXEMPT from the fixed point by construction — never tracked, therefore
# outside it. Left un-ignored, a bundle written into the working tree is an untracked entry
# that no exclusion authority accounts for, so it counts against CLO-01
# (initial_dirty_entries) and CLO-05 (untracked_outside_excluded) and aborts `make rfp-gate`
# before any pipeline stage executes — and it is separately retained by UCOS-RIB-001's
# scoped observation, failing GATE-12 (Repository Clean). Measured consequence of its
# absence: a 92,678,041-byte bundle at the repository root held G-15 CLOSED at
# df763bf while every producer in the declared pipeline was in fact convergent.
# Declared at the GENUS (*.bundle) rather than by filename so recurrence is structurally
# impossible for any future bundle under any name — mirrors the existing
# determinism-evidence/, /knowledge/ and /realization/ generated-artifact policy.
# Bundles belong in durable storage OUTSIDE the repository, never inside the tree they back up.
*.bundle


# UCOS-CL-002/CL-017 — WITHDRAWN: the `* [2-9]` / `* [2-9].*` Finder-duplicate patterns.
#
# They were introduced at be46a300 to stop untracked Finder copies aborting the pre-commit
# ruff hook, and they were unsound in three independent ways:
#
#   1. A filename pattern cannot decide a semantic class. Measured over the 45 matching
#      files actually present: 26 were byte-identical to HEAD, 10 were stale snapshots
#      recoverable from history, 2 held content in no commit, 5 were environmental peers,
#      and 2 were TRACKED AUTHORED sources. Name shape predicted none of that.
#
#   2. The rule matched tracked authored truth. `00-SOURCE/VISION/Missing 2.docx` and
#      `Missing 3.docx` are a numbered series with no `Missing.docx` base; both are tracked
#      and both are matched (`git check-ignore -v --no-index` confirms). They survived only
#      because git does not apply ignore rules to files already in the index — so the moment
#      either left the index it would have vanished from governance. The comment this block
#      replaces asserted the opposite ("intentionally numbered originals are therefore not
#      suppressed"); that assertion was false, and it is the same defect class the
#      P0-FINAL-CONVERGENCE-001 re-admission block above exists to correct.
#
#   3. Most seriously, it manufactured cleanliness. UCOS-RIB-001 measures
#      `dirty_entries_outside_generated` from `git status --porcelain`, so adding these two
#      lines removed 41 physically-present files from the gate's observation surface,
#      flipping GATE-12 and GATE-04, opening `rib.json:gate`, satisfying AEE
#      `OBS-BLUEPRINT-GATE` and clearing `CONV-02` — on a repository that still held every
#      contaminating file. An exclusion rule must never be an input to the gate that polices
#      the excluded state.
#
# The replacement is not another pattern. Duplicate detection is now a CONTENT-derived
# classification owned by UCOS-RIB-001's existing duplicate plane (EXACT_COPY_OF_HEAD /
# STALE_SNAPSHOT / UNIQUE_CONTENT / NO_CANONICAL_PEER / TRACKED_AUTHORED), and repository
# cleanliness is measured over the ignored-inclusive filesystem with every ignored path
# required to resolve to a declared class in the tracked exclusion register
# (`00-BOOK/DATA/exclusion-register.json`). Deletion is a separate authorized disposition,
# never an ignore rule. No pattern is reintroduced here, deliberately: the class is
# platform-neutral and is decided by blob comparison, not by macOS Finder's naming.

# UVI-000001 — the Verification Evidence Registry. A content-addressed CACHE of stage
# results, keyed by digests over content hashes UCOS-UGA-001 already publishes. It is not
# repository truth: deleting the whole store changes no verdict, only the cost of reaching
# one. A cache inside the tracked tree would be a second answer to "did this pass", and
# UCOS-UGA-001 would measure each entry as an unidentified object — which it did, before
# this rule existed.
.ucos-verification-evidence/

# UEG-000001 — the execution environment fingerprint cache and the per-run execution
# evidence. Both describe THIS MACHINE'S environment: an interpreter path, a venv prefix,
# an installed toolchain. None of it reproduces on another machine, so committing it would
# publish a claim that is false everywhere except where it was written. The cache may skip
# exactly one measurement and never a verdict (see the declaration), so deleting the whole
# directory changes no verdict — only the cost of reaching one. The evidence is emitted
# fresh by every certified run and is bound into certification from there, not from git.
.ucos/
.uci-evidence/
coverage_gap_inventory.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# UCOS-UCTX-001 — GENERATED CONTEXT PROJECTIONS (Model B).
#
# Every path below is emitted by 00-BOOK/tools/ukctx.py from the authored
# declaration at 00-BOOK/DATA/context-authority.json. Under Decision-01 a
# projection is a PRODUCT, never tracked truth: the canonical authority is the
# authored source, and a product that is also tracked is a second copy of a
# truth that already exists (UCKP-ART-03) and a permanent identity spent on
# something re-derivable in one command (UCKP-ART-11).
#
# EXCLUSION COSTS A DECLARATION. Every rule here resolves to a
# GENERATED_DETERMINISTIC entry in 00-BOOK/DATA/exclusion-register.json naming
# this producer, its regeneration command and its fixed-point proof. An ignored
# path with no declared class is `ignored_unclassified` and fails closed, so
# these lines REMOVE no obligation — they move it.
#
# A FRESH CLONE HAS NO CONTEXT UNTIL IT GENERATES. That is enforced, not
# assumed: scripts/generate-prerequisites.sh emits them at verify.sh stage 1b,
# and the context gate refuses a tree in which a declared surface is missing.
# Regenerate at any time with: python3 00-BOOK/tools/ukctx.py build
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/00-BOOK/CONTEXT/

# UCOS-UCTX-001 — PHASE 10 CERTIFICATION (Model B, same decision as the projections).
# A measurement ABOUT the context authority, never an input to one. Rebuilt by
# `python3 00-BOOK/tools/ukctx_certify.py`; `--check` refuses a stale one.
/00-BOOK/CONTEXT-CERTIFICATION/
/AGENTS.md
/README.md
/.claude/CLAUDE.md
/.cursor/rules/ucos.mdc
/.kiro/steering/ucos.md
/.github/copilot-instructions.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLAUDE CODE OPERATIONAL STATE (MB9).
#
# These paths were excluded ONLY by non-versioned mechanisms — `.git/info/exclude`
# for most of them and this developer's global `~/.config/git/ignore` for
# settings.local.json. Neither travels with a clone, so the repository's ignore
# posture differed between machines: paths that were excluded here were untracked
# and unignored anywhere else. UCOS-UCTX-001 INV-CTX-12 walks agent directories
# ignored-inclusive, so an unclassified operational file is a gate REFUSAL — which
# turned a per-workstation accident into a failure whose cause was invisible.
#
# Declaring them here makes the exclusion travel with the repository. Every rule
# resolves to a TOOL_OPERATIONAL entry in 00-BOOK/DATA/exclusion-register.json and
# to an agent_surface_rule in 00-BOOK/DATA/context-authority.json, so this REMOVES
# no obligation: an ignored path with no declared class still fails closed.
#
# These are per-developer runtime state — a lock, a mailbox, a daemon's own record
# of itself. They are never shared and never repository truth, which is the same
# class the register already assigns to settings.local.json.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/.claude/settings.local.json
**/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
**/.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
**/.claude/routines/.state/
**/.claude/worktrees/
**/.claude/checkpoints/
**/.claude/mailbox/
**/.claude/agent-registry.json
**/.claude/agent-memory-local
**/.claude/first-run
**/.claude/assistant-daemon-state.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .kilo/ — the Kiro IDE's per-clone operational state.
#
# Same class and same reasoning as the .claude runtime state above: worktrees it
# materialises, agent-manager state, lockfiles. None of it is repository truth, none
# of it is shared, none of it is reproducible across machines — TOOL_OPERATIONAL.
#
# WHY THE DIRECTORY AND NOT JUST THE WORKTREES. `.kilo/worktrees/` was already covered
# by .git/info/exclude, but the context gate (INV-CTX-12) tests the top-level directory
# itself with `git check-ignore -q .kilo`. A rule covering only the subtree leaves the
# root un-ignored, so the gate walked the tree, found instruction-shaped .md files inside
# the worktree copy, and failed closed on an undeclared agent surface. Matching the
# directory is what makes the exclusion register's existing classification visible to
# the discovery leg that looks for it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.kilo/

